// name :
"P1502410321" "The Sky Is Falling"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AdmiralSutterPart1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3764523210" "The Sky Is Falling: Operation Corsair"
// DetailString :
"P3171448217" "Admiral Sutter asked you to volunteer for a classified operation out in the Atlantic Ocean, where the C.S.S. and the U.S. 11th Fleet Freedom Corp Initiative had identified an energy signature that was confirmed to be a Praetorian Rift. You joined a contingent of 11th Fleet naval vessels to investigate the signature and came under attack by a coalition of Sky Raiders and Praetorian Imperial Defense Force soldiers. The source of the attack was a mass of ocean vessels stolen over the years and cobbled together into a sort of floating fortress by the Sky Raiders. The attack on this fortress was fierce, but ultimately the Praetorian Rift was silenced and the commander of the fortress captured.<br><br>Information obtained by fleet specialists determined that a cargo ship had left the Sky Raider flotilla and all evidence suggested that this ship was chock full of Praetorian IDF soldiers and their dreaded Warwalkers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AdmiralSutterPart2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P448242110" "The Sky Is Falling: Operation Boomerang"
// DetailString :
"P2930380360" "Admiral Sutter asked you to volunteer for a classified operation out in the Atlantic Ocean, where the C.S.S. and the U.S. 11th Fleet Freedom Corp Initiative had identified an energy signature that was confirmed to be a Praetorian Rift. You joined a contingent of 11th Fleet naval vessels to investigate the signature and came under attack by a coalition of Sky Raiders and Praetorian Imperial Defense Force soldiers. The source of the attack was a mass of ocean vessels stolen over the years and cobbled together into a sort of floating fortress by the Sky Raiders. The attack on this fortress was fierce, but ultimately the Praetorian Rift was silenced and the commander of the fortress captured.<br><br>Information obtained by fleet specialists determined that a cargo ship had left the Sky Raider flotilla and all evidence suggested that this ship was chock full of Praetorian IDF soldiers and their dreaded Warwalkers. Boarding a helicopter, you made haste toward Paragon City, discovering too late that the Praetorian offensive had already begun on Talos Island. Arriving in the burning port you followed a trail of devastation inland, where you linked up with Luminary and learned that Longbow and the police force had managed to contain the IDF forces inside the main transit tunnel. You moved in to finish the job.<br><br>Instead of finding a massive invasion force you discovered only a token rear guard. The rest of the IDF invaders had moved into the sewer network and were headed toward the mainland under the war walls! Luminary ordered you to pursue and report the position of the IDF forces so that Longbow and Paragon Police could respond before the attackers resurfaced. As you gave chase and arrived beneath Skyway City you felt the ground churn and roll as a powerful earthquake rocked the city above. Luminary informed you that reports were coming in that Skyway City was under attack not only by IDF troops emerging from the sewer system, but by Sky Raider forces supported by high performance combat aircraft. Rushing to put an end to the attack on Skyway you were intercepted by a vile Praetorian Powers Division member named Riptide, and he was backed up by a powerful Seer and grotesque walking cyborg bombs."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - AdmiralSutterSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1379376810" "Tickets To The Admiral's Ball"
// tDetailString :
"P2271037264" "Admiral Sutter gave you these tickets to the Admiral's Ball as thanks for your selfless heroism in the defense of Paragon City during an infamous day where the people of Paragon City were convinced that...<br><br><b>The Sky Is Falling</b><br><br>It began when Admiral Sutter asked you to volunteer for a classified operation out in the Atlantic Ocean, where the C.S.S. and the U.S. 11th Fleet Freedom Corp Initiative had identified an energy signature that was confirmed to be a Praetorian Rift. You joined a contingent of 11th Fleet naval vessels to investigate the signature and came under attack by a coalition of Sky Raiders and Praetorian Imperial Defense Force soldiers. The source of the attack was a mass of ocean vessels stolen over the years and cobbled together into a sort of floating fortress by the Sky Raiders. The attack on this fortress was fierce, but ultimately the Praetorian Rift was silenced and the commander of the fortress captured.<br><br>Information obtained by fleet specialists determined that a cargo ship had left the Sky Raider flotilla and all evidence suggested that this ship was chock full of Praetorian IDF soldiers and their dreaded Warwalkers. Boarding a helicopter, you made haste toward Paragon City, discovering too late that the Praetorian offensive had already begun on Talos Island. Arriving in the burning port you followed a trail of devastation inland, where you linked up with Luminary and learned that Longbow and the police force had managed to contain the IDF forces inside the main transit tunnel. You moved in to finish the job.<br><br>Instead of finding a massive invasion force you discovered only a token rear guard. The rest of the IDF invaders had moved into the sewer network and were headed toward the mainland under the war walls! Luminary ordered you to pursue and report the position of the IDF forces so that Longbow and Paragon Police could respond before the attackers resurfaced. As you gave chase and arrived beneath Skyway City you felt the ground churn and roll as a powerful earthquake rocked the city above. Luminary informed you that reports were coming in that Skyway City was under attack not only by IDF troops emerging from the sewer system, but by Sky Raider forces supported by high performance combat aircraft. Rushing to put an end to the attack on Skyway you were intercepted by a vile Praetorian Powers Division member named Riptide, and he was backed up by a powerful Seer and grotesque walking cyborg bombs. <br><br>Moving into Skyway City proper you felt the ground again lurch and the air choke with dust as the Skyway City freeway system collapsed over your location, threatening to bury you alive. Moving beneath the rubble you encountered two Praetorian super powered individuals who, despite opposing genders, had a striking similarity to the Primal Earth individuals Fusionette and Jim Temblor. You had to defeat the two before they could charge up a third and final earthquake that would bring Skyway City down on top of you all.<br><br>clambering up from the ruins of the Freeway you sought out the masterminds behind the attack on the city; Colonel Duray of the Sky Raiders, and Colonel Duray of the Praetorian Imperial Defense Force. You located the duo coordinating the attack across the city and engaged them in a deadly battle. Ultimately, however, the Praetorian forces and their Sky Raider allies proved to be no match for your abilities. With the attack stymied and their commanders dead or captured, Longbow and the city's combined heroes surrounded and forced the surrender of the scattered and leaderless IDF forces, while the United States Navy pursued and shot down the last of the Sky Raider's high performance fighter aircraft. Though the city burned, the day had been won, all thanks to your valiant efforts in opposing the Praetorian Menace."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - AdmiralSutterDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TalkedToAdmiralSutter Text :
"P580791951" "The Praetorians are due to arrive at Paragon City in a few hours. It would be a miracle if we arrived before them, but I think there is still enough time to hit them before they dig in.<br><br>Good luck, {TaskForceName}. I'm counting on you."
// Answer Text :
"P828938388" "You can count on us, Admiral."
// Page FirstChat Text :
"P2344940834" "Sounds like the Praetorians have already taken an invasion force toward Paragon City. We're beat to hell out here, {HeroName}. Even if we could get the fleet underway immediately it would mean leaving the Donald Cook behind.<br><br>I'm leaving the Mitscher and Stout to handle things here while we're taking the Mason back to Paragon City. Rough seas aside, we should be back there in a few hours, and hopefully in time to stop this damn invasion force of theirs."
// Answer Text :
"P1766416113" "Hopefully it will be in time to stop them."
// Page Page1 Text :
"P548805866" "You won't be alone, {HeroName}. I've alerted Freedom Corps of the situation. Hopefully Longbow and the PPD will be able to stall their assault long enough for your task force to arrive.<br><br>When we arrive back in Independence Port we need to move quickly. Time is no longer a luxury we can afford.<br><br>Oh, and {HeroName}... good hunting."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LuminaryDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TalkedToLuminary Text :
"P4034533938" "Don't worry about Talos Island, {HeroName}. Citadel and I will handle what Praetorian forces remain. You need to go after their main force down in the sewers."
// Answer Text :
"P3736126647" "Understood"
// Page FirstChat Text :
"P596187150" "{HeroName}, I thought you were out with 11th Fleet in the Atlantic."
// Answer Text :
"P206263720" "We just sailed back into port. What's the situation?"
// Page Page1 Text :
"P2399586580" "The Praetorians came into port aboard a cargo vessel. The Port Authority tried to stop them, but their vessel was moving too quickly.<br><br>They ran aground just over there near the ferry parking lot and started disgorging their Warworks battle robots as a vanguard force for their troops."
// Answer Text :
"P3666913225" "There doesn't appear to be much damage for an attack."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P3732511067" "They're leaving most of the civilians alone, unless someone pulls a gun on them, then they respond with deadly force.<br><br>Citadel and I have been trying to organize Longbow and the Talos Island police to deal with the chaos, but War Walkers seem to have spread to every corner of the island in search of heroes to engage and destroy.<br><br>We've managed to corner their main force inside this tunnel, but so far they're so well dug in that we haven't been able to punch more than 200 yards past their defenses. We've been in this stalemate for over an hour now. "
// Answer Text :
"P2928242794" "I take it you're looking for someone to lead the charge."
// Page Page3 Text :
"P1518994358" "I can't ask you to do that, {HeroName}, but, right now you and your task force are the most organized heroes on the island. The sooner we can break the backs of the Praetorian command and control, the sooner this will all be over."
// Answer Text :
"P1446744287" "Are they working with the Sky Raiders?"
// Page Page4 Text :
"P14761828" "No, we have seen no evidence of Sky Raiders working with the Praetorians, but I'll inform Citadel to be alert for their presence. Thank you for the warning."
// Answer Text :
"P933080367" "Tell your men to stand back, we're going in!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1643134626" "I'm leading a small fleet out into the Atlantic to rendezvous with <color red>A Praetorian Rift Signature</color> that we've detected out there. The Joint Chiefs don't want to hear this, but I suspect that this is going to get ugly, and fast. {HeroName}, if the Praetorians are ready for us, and I don't doubt that they are, then I could really use your help on this one.<br><br>Orders are the reconnoiter the rift signature and, if possible, destroy it.<br><br>I have no intention of letting them form a beach head in our world."
// AcceptString :
"P326454943" "Help Admiral Sutter with Operation Corsair"
// SendOffString :
"P2987586256" "Great to have you aboard. You'll sail with me on the USS Mason. She's an Arleigh-Burke class missile destroyer, just like the other three ships in my little recon fleet. She may not be the largest ship in the Navy, but she is a fighter and can sink anything I've ever seen in the water. Heh, let's just hope that the Praetorians don't know how to fly."
// TaskTitle :
"P2273210203" "<color deepskyblue>The Sky Is Falling</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2280269040" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Operation Corsair</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3622965509" "Investigate the Praetorian Rift Signature"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1747982756" "<color deepskyblue>The Sky Is Falling<br>Part One: Operation Corsair<br><br></color>The Fleet is ready to get underway. The longer we wait, the bigger this Praetorian beachhead could get."

